# charon integration step 43 after 546078ea5d: commit edaf3da24157560e40e7694412db17f6911e5735
# first parent a9792e57169669e1353f17fbadb2d03dd995babe
# series charon: patch -p1 in charon/ of the upstream source
#
# charon: partially monomorphized associated items take their parent parameters first
#
# compute_shape visited the explicit region arguments of an item before its type arguments. For a trait
# method, the region of `&mut self` therefore came before the regions found inside the trait arguments.
# For example, FnMut::<_, (&'a mut T1, T2), _>::call_mut had <'self, 'a>, whereas the call_mut of an
# impl takes the impl regions first, as in the generics of every associated item. Consumers that order
# regions by position (the backward functions of Aeneas) then disagreed between the specialized trait
# declaration and its implementations: (closure, arg) versus (arg, closure) in the Lean output of
# Aeneas' SpecializedClosureClauses test (E18-d).
#
# The shape now visits the parent arguments (the trait declaration or implementation arguments of an
# associated item) before the item's own arguments. New UI test: monomorphize-mut-method-region-order.
# The re-blessed monomorphize-mut-{opaque,opaque-hard,clause-order}.out contain only these region
# renumberings. Suite: 325 passed, 3 ignored.
#
# Integrated onto ca6e5e9 (partial monomorphization keeps field projections): monomorphize-mut-opaque(-hard).out
# conflicted with ca6e5e9, which drops the generic closure type from them; both were re-blessed from the
# integrated binary and equal the renumbering above applied to the ca6e5e9 outputs. Suite: 326 passed, 3 ignored.

